# Wiring: `synthorg.api.controllers.{{.Domain}}` controller

Generated by `synthorg new controller {{.Domain}}`. The controller and
service modules are conventions-clean (service-injected via factory,
domain-error translation through `EXCEPTION_HANDLERS`, paginated
list endpoint, structured `API_RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND` log on 404).
The steps below register the controller with the Litestar app and
make sure the consuming repository is exposed on `PersistenceBackend`.

## 1. Register the controller

Add to `src/synthorg/api/app.py` (or the equivalent route registry the
project uses) under the existing `route_handlers` list:

```python
from synthorg.api.controllers.{{.Domain}} import {{.ClassName}}Controller

app = Litestar(
    route_handlers=[
        ...,
        {{.ClassName}}Controller,
    ],
)
```

## 2. Expose the repository on `PersistenceBackend`

The controller calls into `state.app_state.persistence.{{.Domain}}_items`.
If you have not already run `synthorg new persistence {{.Domain}}`, do
that first and follow its WIRING.md to expose the repository. Without
that step the controller raises `AttributeError` on first request.

## 3. Replace placeholder pagination with cursor pagination

The list endpoint currently builds `PaginatedResponse` with
`pagination=None` and a plain `limit / offset` pair. For production
endpoints, switch to the cursor-based pagination already used
elsewhere in the API:

```python
from synthorg.api.pagination import CursorLimit, CursorParam, paginate_cursor

@get(guards=[require_read_access])
async def list_{{.Domain}}_items(
    self,
    state: State,
    cursor: CursorParam = None,
    limit: CursorLimit = 50,
) -> PaginatedResponse[{{.ClassName}}Item]:
    items = await _service(state).list_items(limit=limit + 1, offset=0)
    page, meta = paginate_cursor(
        items, limit=limit, cursor=cursor,
        secret=state.app_state.cursor_secret,
    )
    return PaginatedResponse[{{.ClassName}}Item](data=page, pagination=meta)
```

The cursor secret is mandatory (the backend refuses to start without
``SYNTHORG_PAGINATION_CURSOR_SECRET`` set), so `paginate_cursor`
always has a secret to sign tokens with.
